Australia has become the latest  continent to confirm a case of the  coronavirus which originated in China  three cases have also now been found in  Europe all three appeared in France in  the capital Paris and in the city of  Bordeaux health officials there said a  48 year old patient had been travelling  through China and passed through Wuhan  that's the epicenter of the outbreak  Frances Health Minister said authorities  are not ruling out finding new cases we  are going to do everything possible to  contain this epidemic knowing that it is  possible and even probable that there  will be other cases particularly in  Europe just because there aren't any  other identified cases today doesn't  mean that no other cases are circulating  meanwhile here are the latest numbers in  China the virus has now killed at least  41 people with more than 1300 others  affected authorities are taking  unprecedented measures to try to stop  the spread of the virus travel  restrictions remain in place and over a  dozen cities in China and all of the  countries 70,000 movie theaters have  also been closed the actions are urgent  as millions are on the move over the  Lunar New Year holiday as the scale of  the outbreak grows so too does the  urgency of the response in Wuhan  construction is underway on a new  hospital for coronavirus patients  Chinese authorities say it will be  complete in just over a week the city at  the outbreaks epicenter remains under a  transport lockdown Road checks drivers  with a high temperature are sent to  hospital across China almost 40 million  people face travel restrictions during  the important New Year holiday a lot of  people had no way to get home I really  feel for them because I can understand  what it's like to have been working hard  away from home for a year everyone looks  forward to being with their family but  in this situation there's really nothing  we can do  the outbreak even featured on state  televisions Lunar New Year broadcast  with hosts sending messages of support  to medical staff in airports across the  globe scenes like this are becoming  common officials using thermal monitors  to screen travelers for signs of fever  around the world concern is heating up  well we have team coverage on the spread  of that virus I'm joined now by DW  correspondent Lisa Lewis she is in Paris  and Fabien Kretschmer in Beijing for us  we want to start with Lisa Lisa the  first European cases of the virus have  now been confirmed those are in France  what more can you tell us about the  situation there in those infections well  the authorities have said that all these  three people recently traveled to China  and then came back one person for 48  year old man in Bordeaux in southwestern  France he apparently is from China he's  French he has French nationality he went  to see SOS mid-sized which is an  overnight doctor service over over the  weekend and they very quickly identified  symptoms and also when they learned that  he was actually from Wuhan where the  virus comes from really they put him on  - under quarantine and transferred him  to hospital the authorities here are  saying that two more cases have been  detected in Paris it looks like it was  first one person then someone else who  had been in touch with that person  obviously the authorities are trying to  reassure everybody and saying we've got  everything in place to deal with this  especially as we had to deal with other  diseases that were similar in the past  okay Fabien crutch for now in Beijing  it's the Chinese New Year today but  celebrations not taking place as usual  how is China responding yeah I'm in  Beijing right now and here every I'm the  public gatherings they've been canceled  also the tourist attractions have been  closed - part of also of the Chinese  wall have been closed and there  definitely doesn't feel like the typical  Chinese New Year usually it's also the  season where domestic spending is really  high but now  people prefer to stay at home they don't  go to restaurants they don't spend so  much on gifts for their families so yeah  it definitely feels quite different in  them if you ask the population then  especially among the young there's also  some kind of anger against the local  authorities in Wuhan in in in Hubei  Province because just two days before  they shut down the city you know shut  down all the transportation they were  attending lavish singing song dinners  and they really cannot understand well  the party authorities tell the people to  wear face masks and to avoid all public  gatherings but of course they themselves  are quite differently Lisa what about  there in France what measures are French  authorities taking to stop the spread of  the virus now that we are seeing the  first cases appearing there well the  authorities have said that they are well  prepared there are three specific  hospitals in Paris they are prepared to  deal with such infectious diseases the  Health Minister Anna's Bazar has said  yesterday that people if they had  similar symptoms that they shouldn't go  to see someone at the hospital or  contact their local GP there's a special  helpline they need to call and then  people will come and make some tests at  their home and then maybe bring them to  specialised services obviously the  Health Minister said that she would give  a daily update on the situation she said  they're probably going to be more cases  like this in France and she also said  that probably these cases were first  detected in France because France had  developed as one of the first countries  a method to detect the virus now people  here obviously quite concerned about  this as you look at social media they're  really wondering why there aren't  systematic checks at airports because  there are people who've talked to French  media in the past saying you know I just  got home from kleiner and no one  actually checked me no one controlled me  alright Lisa Lewis with the latest there  in Paris and Fabien Karishma for us in  Beijing thank you to you both
 

